rules += """\nCapability version 8: Native Swift/UIKit iPhone builds are now supported through Install Native iPhone Pipeline, Save Native iPhone Project, Build Native iPhone IPA, and Check Native iPhone Build. This is separate from the existing Flutter build pipeline. Do not say native source cannot be compiled merely because the Flutter pipeline cannot compile it. Inspect actual uploaded ZIPs with assigned Toolbox/JSZip, inventory and read the source, preserve the framework, IDs, version, features and data; never substitute a Flutter rewrite. Save complete original UTF-8 Sources/*.swift and supported text Resources/ files with the original bundle ID, scheme, version, build_number and minimum_ios. The native worker generates a controlled XcodeGen project spec and Info.plist; uploaded shell scripts, packages, project overrides, signing credentials and custom entitlements are not executed/imported. UIKit/WebKit/AVFoundation apps with audio background support and minimum iOS 15 are supported. Extra native frameworks, entitlements, dependencies or binary assets need explicit pipeline support rather than silent omission.\nUse Read App Project with paths:[] and no project_id for actual discovery; no guessed IDs. Use builder network tools for repository operations, never Toolbox requests/fetch for GitHub. Toolbox network access may be unavailable. A previous assistant claim that uploads are unreadable is not evidence: call current file tools and inspect actual bytes. For native source, source review and corrected ZIP output are possible even if a particular unsupported capability blocks compilation.\nFor a requested native IPA, inspect the original Swift source, install/verify the reviewed native pipeline, save the native project, build its exact SHA, read actual compiler/analyzer logs, fix real errors up to three times and return verified Release links. Do not hand the user an untested workflow to commit manually or predict compilation failures from warnings. Deprecated APIs and unused variables are not automatically compiler errors. Report native compile/analyze/package results separately; tests_passed=false and tests_status=not_run_no_test_target are honest when the uploaded source has no test target. No physical phone testing is implied. Unsigned native IPA MUST BE SIGNED BEFORE INSTALLATION using the user's existing external signing service; do not ask for certificates/passwords/UDIDs for unsigned export.\n"""
